totaldrop (0.3.0~beta.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Send a text instead of files: "Send text" on the Send screen, or
    "Send clipboard" in the app's launcher menu. A text that arrives is
    shown, not saved, with any hidden characters named, and "Copy text"
    copies it exactly as it came. The command line can send a text too:
    totaldrop send --text "...", or totaldrop send - for standard input.
  * "Send with TotalDrop" in the right-click menu of Dolphin, Files
    (once python3-nautilus is installed) and Nemo; "Send files" and
    "Receive files" when you right-click TotalDrop in the taskbar or app
    launcher.
  * Software centres describe TotalDrop in all 35 languages of the app.
  * The right-click menu of text fields is in the app's language where Qt
    draws it (Qt 6.11 and later), and Qt's own windows follow
    right-to-left languages.
  * Settings says that codes and verification words stay in English, so
    that two devices set to different languages show the same words.
  * Security: a sending device no longer connects to its relay when the
    receiving device uses a different relay or none, so that relay no
    longer sees the sender's IP address. A receiver on 0.1 set to another
    relay now needs a direct path.
  * Security: when a send or receive fails on the command line, control
    characters in the error's detail are named instead of passed to the
    terminal (GHSA-c6jh-7p7q-8gg4).

 -- TotalDrop <hello@totaldrop.app>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:02:49 +0300

totaldrop (0.3.0~beta.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The translations built into the app are now under MIT OR Apache-2.0.
    The package's copyright file says so for the translations and the
    library that compiles them, and no longer repeats its licence
    paragraphs.
  * In the packages the project builds, the app's built-in Qt resources
    no longer carry the time they were built, so two builds of the same
    source come out the same there.

 -- TotalDrop <hello@totaldrop.app>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0300

totaldrop (0.3.0~beta.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A transfer that started on a direct connection no longer stops with
    "timed out" when that path goes quiet, for example when Wi-Fi drops:
    after 8 seconds without anything from the other device it moves onto the
    relay and goes on. Both devices must use the same relay.
  * A transfer through the relay survives a connection that dies without
    either end noticing, for example after switching Wi-Fi networks: the
    device notices within 10 seconds and connects again.
  * The sending device's progress bar shows what has reached the other
    device, instead of running ahead and showing a file as sent while it is
    still on the way.
  * When a transfer fails, the reason is now given in your language for many
    failures, under Details. The technical message stays in English for
    problem reports and is labelled as such.

 -- TotalDrop <hello@totaldrop.app>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0300

totaldrop (0.3.0~beta.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Opening files with TotalDrop while it is already open, for example with
    "Open with" in a file manager, adds them to the open window instead of
    starting a second one, and the window comes to the front.
  * A transfer through the relay connects even when the relay is slow to get
    going, instead of failing after 20 seconds, and reconnects when the
    relay closes the connection. It is also faster when the relay is far
    away.
  * A transfer no longer sometimes stops right after the code is entered,
    with "the other side left" on the sending device.
  * Stop on the sending device now cuts the transfer at once; files still
    being sent when you press Stop are no longer completed and kept on the
    receiving device.

 -- TotalDrop <hello@totaldrop.app>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 08:30:00 +0300

totaldrop (0.3.0~beta.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * On GNOME and on Hyprland without a Qt theme, the window takes the
    colours of your GTK theme and follows a theme change at once; buttons,
    fields and switches take the desktop's shape. Omarchy keeps its own
    theme.
  * Clearer messages: a code nobody is using, a code that expired and a
    server address that is not valid are each named as such.
  * Pasting the whole share message into the receive field finds the code in
    it, invisible characters such as direction marks are dropped from a
    pasted code, and codes typed with Arabic, Persian or Urdu digits are
    accepted. In a right-to-left language the shared message shows the code
    in order.
  * The screens stay centred in a wide window and files in the Send list get
    an icon for their kind. Escape goes back from Send, Receive and
    Settings, Enter presses the focused button on the result screen, and Tab
    reaches controls it used to skip, scrolling them into view.
  * With some Mesa drivers (seen on Intel graphics) the window no longer
    falls back to 16-bit colour, so its colours are no longer a shade off.
  * totaldrop-desktop --help and --version print to the terminal instead of
    opening the window.

